ing section: `DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar(lambda v: _int_or_none_min(v, 32))`. Better use a factory method to be idiomatic. I'll add a static factory `int_or_none_min(*, minimum: int)` in EnvVar.\n\nNow logger.py:\n\n```python\n_OMITTED_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\n\ndef _truncate_message(message, max_chars):\n    if max_chars is None or len(message) <= max_chars:\n        return message\n    available = max_chars - len(_OMITTED_MARKER)\n    head = (available + 1) // 2\n    tail = available - head\n    return message[:head] + _OMITTED_MARKER + (message[len(message)-tail:] if tail else \"\")\n```\n\nWait budget 32: marker len 15, available 17, head = ceil(17/2)=9, tail=8. Matches example. Good.\n\nFormatter __init__:\n\n```python\n    def __init__(self, fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False, *, max_message_chars: int | None = None) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        if max_message_chars is not None:\n            if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int) or max_message_chars < 32:\n                raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be None or an int >= 32, got {max_message_chars!r}\")\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n        self.max_message_chars = max_message_chars\n```\n\nCareful: bool check first — isinstance(True, int) is True, so must reject bool. The test likely passes value like \"64\" string → ValueError, 64.0 float → ValueError, True → ValueError.\n\nformat:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record):\n        if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            original_message = record.message\n            # compute message after args substitution without mutating record\n            ...\n```\n\nApproach: call `record.getMessage()` to get fully substituted message. Then truncate; then temporarily set record.msg = truncated, record.args = (), call super().format(record), and restore in finally.\n\nBut careful: record.message attribute — logging.Formatter.format sets record.message = record.getMessage(). We set msg temporarily; format will compute message from msg. After format, restore record.msg, record.args, and record.message.\n\nImplementation:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        max_chars = self.max_message_chars\n        if max_chars is None or getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True:\n            return self._format_with_prefix(record)\n        message = record.getMessage()\n        if len(message) <= max_chars:\n            return self._format_with_prefix(record)\n        truncated = _truncate(message, max_chars)\n        saved = (record.msg, record.args, getattr(record, \"message\", None))\n        record.msg = truncated\n        record.args = ()\n        try:\n            return self._format_with_prefix(record)\n        finally:\n            record.msg, record.args = saved[0], saved[1]\n            if saved[2] is None:\n                ... \n```\n\nHmm record.message restore: since format() sets it anyway to truncated message. Better: after restoring msg/args, delete record.message or restore to saved value. But if saved[2] was set (from earlier handler formatting), restore it. If not present originally, delete. Use try/except AttributeError. Actually simpler: keep it simple:\n\n```python\n        try:\n            return self._format_with_prefix(record)\n        finally:\n            record.msg = saved_msg\n            record.args = saved_args\n            if hasattr(record, \"message\") ... \n```\n\nBut careful: `_format_with_prefix` may raise; finally handles.\n\nAlso note record.message — after our format, super().format sets record.message = truncated. Another handler without budget (e.g., a full handler) that calls format again would recompute message from record.msg — restored, so fine. But the task says \"同一记录随后交给完整处理器，仍须保留完整消息\". Resto